---
/**
 * The 60× showcase. Visualizes the before/after: a flat 12k-token
 * memory file vs CtxOne's 200-token budgeted recall for the same
 * topic. Pure CSS — no JavaScript, no framework.
 */
---

<section class="section">
	<div class="container">
		<h2 class="section-title">The 60× number, provable in real time</h2>
		<p class="section-lede">
			Every <code>recall</code> response includes a
			<code>_ctxone_stats</code> field showing exactly how many tokens
			you sent vs how many you would have sent if the model had seen
			the full memory graph. This isn't marketing — it's the live
			delta the Hub computes on every request.
		</p>

		<div class="compare">
			<div class="col col-flat">
				<div class="label">Flat memory</div>
				<div class="caption">What the model sees without CtxOne</div>
				<div class="bar bar-flat">
					<span class="bar-inner"></span>
				</div>
				<div class="number number-flat">12,000 tokens</div>
				<div class="note">Every session, every time</div>
			</div>

			<div class="arrow">→</div>

			<div class="col col-ctx">
				<div class="label">CtxOne recall</div>
				<div class="caption">What the model sees with CtxOne</div>
				<div class="bar bar-ctx">
					<span class="bar-inner"></span>
				</div>
				<div class="number number-ctx">200 tokens</div>
				<div class="note">Topic-matched + pinned</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="ratio">
			<span class="x">60×</span>
			<span class="x-label">savings ratio</span>
		</div>

		<p class="footnote">
			Shown: a mature graph of a few hundred facts, recalled for a
			specific topic. On a fresh graph the ratio is close to 1× — it
			grows with the graph, because that's how selective retrieval
			works. <a href="/how-it-works/token-savings/">See the math →</a>
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.compare {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 2rem;
		margin: 2.5rem 0 2rem 0;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}

	.col {
		flex: 1;
		min-width: 14rem;
		background: var(--ctx-panel);
		border: 1px solid var(--ctx-border);
		border-radius: var(--ctx-radius-lg);
		padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
	}

	.label {
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		color: var(--ctx-text-faint);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	.caption {
		color: var(--ctx-text-dim);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.bar {
		height: 1.1rem;
		background: #050505;
		border: 1px solid var(--ctx-border-lo);
		border-radius: var(--ctx-radius-sm);
		overflow: hidden;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.bar-inner {
		display: block;
		height: 100%;
	}

	.bar-flat .bar-inner {
		width: 100%;
		background: repeating-linear-gradient(
			45deg,
			#ef4444,
			#ef4444 8px,
			#c0392b 8px,
			#c0392b 16px
		);
	}

	.bar-ctx .bar-inner {
		width: 1.7%;
		background: var(--ctx-accent);
	}

	.number {
		font-family: var(--ctx-font-mono);
		font-size: 1.4rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: #ffffff;
	}

	.number-ctx {
		color: var(--ctx-accent-text);
	}

	.note {
		color: var(--ctx-text-faint);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		margin-top: 0.25rem;
	}

	.arrow {
		font-size: 2rem;
		color: var(--ctx-text-faint);
		flex-shrink: 0;
	}

	.ratio {
		display: flex;
		align-items: baseline;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem 0;
	}

	.x {
		font-family: var(--ctx-font-mono);
		font-size: 4rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		color: var(--ctx-accent);
		line-height: 1;
	}

	.x-label {
		color: var(--ctx-text-dim);
		font-size: 1rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
	}

	.footnote {
		color: var(--ctx-text-dim);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		max-width: 36rem;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.footnote code,
	.section-lede code {
		background: var(--ctx-panel);
		border: 1px solid var(--ctx-border);
		padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
		border-radius: var(--ctx-radius-sm);
		font-size: 0.9em;
		color: var(--ctx-accent-text);
		font-family: var(--ctx-font-mono);
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.compare {
			flex-direction: column;
		}
		.arrow {
			transform: rotate(90deg);
		}
		.x {
			font-size: 3rem;
		}
	}
</style>
